1:---
2:title: Mutating Data
3:description: Learn how to mutate data using Server Functions and Server Actions in Next.js.
4:related:
5:  title: API Reference
6:  description: Learn more about the features mentioned in this page by reading the API Reference.
7:  links:
8:    - app/api-reference/functions/revalidatePath
9:    - app/api-reference/functions/revalidateTag
10:    - app/api-reference/functions/redirect
11:---
12:
13:You can mutate data in Next.js using [React Server Functions](https://react.dev/reference/rsc/server-functions). This page will go through how you can [create](#creating-server-functions) and [invoke](#invoking-server-functions) Server Functions.
14:
15:## What are Server Functions?
16:
17:A **Server Function** is an asynchronous function that runs on the server. You can call them from the client through a network request, which is why they must be asynchronous.
18:
19:In an `action` or mutation context, they are also called **Server Actions**.
20:
21:By convention, a Server Action is an async function used with [`startTransition`](https://react.dev/reference/react/startTransition). This happens automatically when the function is:
22:
23:- Passed to a `<form>` using the `action` prop.
24:- Passed to a `<button>` using the `formAction` prop.
25:
26:When an action is invoked, Next.js can return both the updated UI and new data in a single server roundtrip.
27:
28:Behind the scenes, actions use the `POST` method, and only this HTTP method can invoke them.
29:
30:> [!WARNING]
31:> Server Functions are reachable via direct POST requests, not just through your application's UI. Always verify authentication and authorization inside every Server Function. See the [Data Security guide](/docs/app/guides/data-security#authentication-and-authorization) for recommended patterns.
32:
33:> **Good to know:** A Server Action is a Server Function used in a specific way (for handling form submissions and mutations). Server Function is the broader term.
34:
35:## Creating Server Functions
36:
37:A Server Function can be defined by using the [`use server`](https://react.dev/reference/rsc/use-server) directive. You can place the directive at the top of an **asynchronous** function to mark the function as a Server Function, or at the top of a separate file to mark all exports of that file.
38:
39:```ts filename="app/lib/actions.ts" switcher
40:import { auth } from '@/lib/auth'
41:
42:export async function createPost(formData: FormData) {
43:  'use server'
44:  const session = await auth()
45:  if (!session?.user) {
46:    throw new Error('Unauthorized')
47:  }
48:
49:  const title = formData.get('title')
50:  const content = formData.get('content')
51:
52:  // Mutate data
53:  // Revalidate cache
54:}
55:
56:export async function deletePost(formData: FormData) {
57:  'use server'
58:  const session = await auth()
59:  if (!session?.user) {
60:    throw new Error('Unauthorized')
61:  }
62:
63:  const id = formData.get('id')
64:
65:  // Verify the user owns this resource before deleting
66:  // Mutate data
67:  // Revalidate cache
68:}
69:```
70:
71:```js filename="app/lib/actions.js" switcher
72:import { auth } from '@/lib/auth'
73:
74:export async function createPost(formData) {
75:  'use server'
76:  const session = await auth()
77:  if (!session?.user) {
78:    throw new Error('Unauthorized')
79:  }
80:
81:  const title = formData.get('title')
82:  const content = formData.get('content')
83:
84:  // Mutate data
85:  // Revalidate cache
86:}
87:
88:export async function deletePost(formData) {
89:  'use server'
90:  const session = await auth()
91:  if (!session?.user) {
92:    throw new Error('Unauthorized')
93:  }
94:
95:  const id = formData.get('id')
96:
97:  // Verify the user owns this resource before deleting
98:  // Mutate data
99:  // Revalidate cache
100:}
101:```
102:
103:### Server Components
104:
105:Server Functions can be inlined in Server Components by adding the `"use server"` directive to the top of the function body:
106:
107:```tsx filename="app/page.tsx" switcher
108:export default function Page() {
109:  // Server Action
110:  async function createPost(formData: FormData) {
111:    'use server'
112:    // ...
113:  }
114:
115:  return <></>
116:}
117:```
118:
119:```jsx filename="app/page.js" switcher
120:export default function Page() {
121:  // Server Action
122:  async function createPost(formData) {
123:    'use server'
124:    // ...
125:  }
126:
127:  return <></>
128:}
129:```
130:
131:> **Good to know:** Server Components support progressive enhancement by default, meaning forms that call Server Actions will be submitted even if JavaScript hasn't loaded yet or is disabled.
132:
133:### Client Components
134:
135:It's not possible to define Server Functions in Client Components. However, you can invoke them in Client Components by importing them from a file that has the `"use server"` directive at the top of it:
136:
137:```ts filename="app/actions.ts" switcher
138:'use server'
139:
140:export async function createPost() {}
141:```
142:
143:```js filename="app/actions.js" switcher
144:'use server'
145:
146:export async function createPost() {}
147:```
148:
149:```tsx filename="app/ui/button.tsx" switcher
150:'use client'
151:
152:import { createPost } from '@/app/actions'
153:
154:export function Button() {
155:  return <button formAction={createPost}>Create</button>
156:}
157:```
158:
159:```jsx filename="app/ui/button.js" switcher
160:'use client'
161:
162:import { createPost } from '@/app/actions'
163:
164:export function Button() {
165:  return <button formAction={createPost}>Create</button>
166:}
167:```
168:
169:> **Good to know:** In Client Components, forms invoking Server Actions will queue submissions if JavaScript isn't loaded yet, and will be prioritized for hydration. After hydration, the browser does not refresh on form submission.
170:
171:### Passing actions as props
172:
173:You can also pass an action to a Client Component as a prop:
174:
175:```jsx
176:<ClientComponent updateItemAction={updateItem} />
177:```
178:
179:```tsx filename="app/client-component.tsx" switcher
180:'use client'
181:
182:export default function ClientComponent({
183:  updateItemAction,
184:}: {
185:  updateItemAction: (formData: FormData) => void
186:}) {
187:  return <form action={updateItemAction}>{/* ... */}</form>
188:}
189:```
190:
191:```jsx filename="app/client-component.js" switcher
192:'use client'
193:
194:export default function ClientComponent({ updateItemAction }) {
195:  return <form action={updateItemAction}>{/* ... */}</form>
196:}
197:```
198:
199:## Invoking Server Functions
200:
201:There are two main ways you can invoke a Server Function:
202:
203:1. [Forms](#forms) in Server and Client Components
204:2. [Event Handlers](#event-handlers) and [useEffect](#useeffect) in Client Components
205:
206:> **Good to know:** Server Functions are designed for server-side mutations. The client currently dispatches and awaits them one at a time. This is an implementation detail and may change. If you need parallel data fetching, use [data fetching](/docs/app/getting-started/fetching-data#server-components) in Server Components, or perform parallel work inside a single Server Function or [Route Handler](/docs/app/guides/backend-for-frontend#manipulating-data).
207:
208:### Forms
209:
210:React extends the HTML [`<form>`](https://react.dev/reference/react-dom/components/form) element to allow a Server Function to be invoked with the HTML `action` prop.
211:
212:When invoked in a form, the function automatically receives the [`FormData`](https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/API/FormData/FormData) object. You can extract the data using the native [`FormData` methods](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/FormData#instance_methods):
213:
214:```tsx filename="app/ui/form.tsx" switcher
215:import { createPost } from '@/app/actions'
216:
217:export function Form() {
218:  return (
219:    <form action={createPost}>
220:      <input type="text" name="title" />
221:      <input type="text" name="content" />
222:      <button type="submit">Create</button>
223:    </form>
224:  )
225:}
226:```
227:
228:```jsx filename="app/ui/form.js" switcher
229:import { createPost } from '@/app/actions'
230:
231:export function Form() {
232:  return (
233:    <form action={createPost}>
234:      <input type="text" name="title" />
235:      <input type="text" name="content" />
236:      <button type="submit">Create</button>
237:    </form>
238:  )
239:}
240:```
241:
242:```ts filename="app/actions.ts" switcher
243:'use server'
244:
245:import { auth } from '@/lib/auth'
246:
247:export async function createPost(formData: FormData) {
248:  const session = await auth()
249:  if (!session?.user) {
250:    throw new Error('Unauthorized')
251:  }
252:
253:  const title = formData.get('title')
254:  const content = formData.get('content')
255:
256:  // Mutate data
257:  // Revalidate cache
258:}
259:```
260:
261:```js filename="app/actions.js" switcher
262:'use server'
263:
264:import { auth } from '@/lib/auth'
265:
266:export async function createPost(formData) {
267:  const session = await auth()
268:  if (!session?.user) {
269:    throw new Error('Unauthorized')
270:  }
271:
272:  const title = formData.get('title')
273:  const content = formData.get('content')
274:
275:  // Mutate data
276:  // Revalidate cache
277:}
278:```
279:
280:### Event Handlers
281:
282:You can invoke a Server Function in a Client Component by using event handlers such as `onClick`.
283:
284:```tsx filename="app/like-button.tsx" switcher
285:'use client'
286:
287:import { incrementLike } from './actions'
288:import { useState } from 'react'
289:
290:export default function LikeButton({ initialLikes }: { initialLikes: number }) {
291:  const [likes, setLikes] = useState(initialLikes)
292:
293:  return (
294:    <>
295:      <p>Total Likes: {likes}</p>
296:      <button
297:        onClick={async () => {
298:          const updatedLikes = await incrementLike()
299:          setLikes(updatedLikes)
300:        }}
301:      >
302:        Like
303:      </button>
304:    </>
305:  )
306:}
307:```
308:
309:```jsx filename="app/like-button.js" switcher
310:'use client'
311:
312:import { incrementLike } from './actions'
313:import { useState } from 'react'
314:
315:export default function LikeButton({ initialLikes }) {
316:  const [likes, setLikes] = useState(initialLikes)
317:
318:  return (
319:    <>
320:      <p>Total Likes: {likes}</p>
321:      <button
322:        onClick={async () => {
323:          const updatedLikes = await incrementLike()
324:          setLikes(updatedLikes)
325:        }}
326:      >
327:        Like
328:      </button>
329:    </>
330:  )
331:}
332:```
333:
334:## Examples
335:
336:### Showing a pending state
337:
338:While executing a Server Function, you can show a loading indicator with React's [`useActionState`](https://react.dev/reference/react/useActionState) hook. This hook returns a `pending` boolean:
339:
340:```tsx filename="app/ui/button.tsx" switcher
341:'use client'
342:
343:import { useActionState, startTransition } from 'react'
344:import { createPost } from '@/app/actions'
345:import { LoadingSpinner } from '@/app/ui/loading-spinner'
346:
347:export function Button() {
348:  const [state, action, pending] = useActionState(createPost, false)
349:
350:  return (
351:    <button onClick={() => startTransition(action)}>
352:      {pending ? <LoadingSpinner /> : 'Create Post'}
353:    </button>
354:  )
355:}
356:```
357:
358:```jsx filename="app/ui/button.js" switcher
359:'use client'
360:
361:import { useActionState, startTransition } from 'react'
362:import { createPost } from '@/app/actions'
363:import { LoadingSpinner } from '@/app/ui/loading-spinner'
364:
365:export function Button() {
366:  const [state, action, pending] = useActionState(createPost, false)
367:
368:  return (
369:    <button onClick={() => startTransition(action)}>
370:      {pending ? <LoadingSpinner /> : 'Create Post'}
371:    </button>
372:  )
373:}
374:```
375:
376:### Refresh data
377:
378:After a mutation, you may want to refresh the current page to show the latest data. You can do this by calling [`refresh`](/docs/app/api-reference/functions/refresh) from `next/cache` in a Server Action:
379:
380:```ts filename="app/lib/actions.ts" switcher
381:'use server'
382:
383:import { auth } from '@/lib/auth'
384:import { refresh } from 'next/cache'
385:
386:export async function updatePost(formData: FormData) {
387:  const session = await auth()
388:  if (!session?.user) {
389:    throw new Error('Unauthorized')
390:  }
391:  // Mutate data
392:  // ...
393:
394:  refresh()
395:}
396:```
397:
398:```js filename="app/lib/actions.js" switcher
399:'use server'
400:
401:import { auth } from '@/lib/auth'
402:import { refresh } from 'next/cache'
403:
404:export async function updatePost(formData) {
405:  const session = await auth()
406:  if (!session?.user) {
407:    throw new Error('Unauthorized')
408:  }
409:  // Mutate data
410:  // ...
411:
412:  refresh()
413:}
414:```
415:
416:This refreshes the client router, ensuring the UI reflects the latest state. The `refresh()` function does not revalidate tagged data. To revalidate tagged data, use [`updateTag`](/docs/app/api-reference/functions/updateTag) or [`revalidateTag`](/docs/app/api-reference/functions/revalidateTag) instead.
417:
418:### Revalidate data
419:
420:After performing a mutation, you can revalidate the Next.js cache and show the updated data by calling [`revalidatePath`](/docs/app/api-reference/functions/revalidatePath) or [`revalidateTag`](/docs/app/api-reference/functions/revalidateTag) within the Server Function:
421:
422:```ts filename="app/lib/actions.ts" switcher
423:import { auth } from '@/lib/auth'
424:import { revalidatePath } from 'next/cache'
425:
426:export async function createPost(formData: FormData) {
427:  'use server'
428:  const session = await auth()
429:  if (!session?.user) {
430:    throw new Error('Unauthorized')
431:  }
432:  // Mutate data
433:  // ...
434:
435:  revalidatePath('/posts')
436:}
437:```
438:
439:```js filename="app/actions.js" switcher
440:import { auth } from '@/lib/auth'
441:import { revalidatePath } from 'next/cache'
442:
443:export async function createPost(formData) {
444:  'use server'
445:  const session = await auth()
446:  if (!session?.user) {
447:    throw new Error('Unauthorized')
448:  }
449:  // Mutate data
450:  // ...
451:  revalidatePath('/posts')
452:}
453:```
454:
455:### Redirect after a mutation
456:
457:You may want to redirect the user to a different page after a mutation. You can do this by calling [`redirect`](/docs/app/api-reference/functions/redirect) within the Server Function.
458:
459:```ts filename="app/lib/actions.ts" switcher
460:'use server'
461:
462:import { auth } from '@/lib/auth'
463:import { revalidatePath } from 'next/cache'
464:import { redirect } from 'next/navigation'
465:
466:export async function createPost(formData: FormData) {
467:  const session = await auth()
468:  if (!session?.user) {
469:    throw new Error('Unauthorized')
470:  }
471:  // Mutate data
472:  // ...
473:
474:  revalidatePath('/posts')
475:  redirect('/posts')
476:}
477:```
478:
479:```js filename="app/actions.js" switcher
480:'use server'
481:
482:import { auth } from '@/lib/auth'
483:import { revalidatePath } from 'next/cache'
484:import { redirect } from 'next/navigation'
485:
486:export async function createPost(formData) {
487:  const session = await auth()
488:  if (!session?.user) {
489:    throw new Error('Unauthorized')
490:  }
491:  // Mutate data
492:  // ...
493:
494:  revalidatePath('/posts')
495:  redirect('/posts')
496:}
497:```
498:
499:Calling `redirect` [throws](/docs/app/api-reference/functions/redirect#behavior) a framework handled control-flow exception. Any code after it won't execute. If you need fresh data, call [`revalidatePath`](/docs/app/api-reference/functions/revalidatePath) or [`revalidateTag`](/docs/app/api-reference/functions/revalidateTag) beforehand.
500:
501:### Cookies
502:
503:You can `get`, `set`, and `delete` cookies inside a Server Action using the [`cookies`](/docs/app/api-reference/functions/cookies) API.
504:
505:When you [set or delete](/docs/app/api-reference/functions/cookies#understanding-cookie-behavior-in-server-functions) a cookie in a Server Action, Next.js re-renders the current page and its layouts on the server so the **UI reflects the new cookie value**.
506:
507:> **Good to know**: The server update applies to the current React tree, re-rendering, mounting, or unmounting components, as needed. Client state is preserved for re-rendered components, and effects re-run if their dependencies changed.
508:
509:```ts filename="app/actions.ts" switcher
510:'use server'
511:
512:import { cookies } from 'next/headers'
513:
514:export async function exampleAction() {
515:  const cookieStore = await cookies()
516:
517:  // Get cookie
518:  cookieStore.get('name')?.value
519:
520:  // Set cookie
521:  cookieStore.set('name', 'Delba')
522:
523:  // Delete cookie
524:  cookieStore.delete('name')
525:}
526:```
527:
528:```js filename="app/actions.js" switcher
529:'use server'
530:
531:import { cookies } from 'next/headers'
532:
533:export async function exampleAction() {
534:  // Get cookie
535:  const cookieStore = await cookies()
536:
537:  // Get cookie
538:  cookieStore.get('name')?.value
539:
540:  // Set cookie
541:  cookieStore.set('name', 'Delba')
542:
543:  // Delete cookie
544:  cookieStore.delete('name')
545:}
546:```
547:
548:### useEffect
549:
550:You can use the React [`useEffect`](https://react.dev/reference/react/useEffect) hook to invoke a Server Action when the component mounts or a dependency changes. This is useful for mutations that depend on global events or need to be triggered automatically. For example, `onKeyDown` for app shortcuts, an intersection observer hook for infinite scrolling, or when the component mounts to update a view count:
551:
552:```tsx filename="app/view-count.tsx" switcher
553:'use client'
554:
555:import { incrementViews } from './actions'
556:import { useState, useEffect, useTransition } from 'react'
557:
558:export default function ViewCount({ initialViews }: { initialViews: number }) {
559:  const [views, setViews] = useState(initialViews)
560:  const [isPending, startTransition] = useTransition()
561:
562:  useEffect(() => {
563:    startTransition(async () => {
564:      const updatedViews = await incrementViews()
565:      setViews(updatedViews)
566:    })
567:  }, [])
568:
569:  // You can use `isPending` to give users feedback
570:  return <p>Total Views: {views}</p>
571:}
572:```
573:
574:```jsx filename="app/view-count.js" switcher
575:'use client'
576:
577:import { incrementViews } from './actions'
578:import { useState, useEffect, useTransition } from 'react'
579:
580:export default function ViewCount({ initialViews }) {
581:  const [views, setViews] = useState(initialViews)
582:  const [isPending, startTransition] = useTransition()
583:
584:  useEffect(() => {
585:    startTransition(async () => {
586:      const updatedViews = await incrementViews()
587:      setViews(updatedViews)
588:    })
589:  }, [])
590:
591:  // You can use `isPending` to give users feedback
592:  return <p>Total Views: {views}</p>
593:}
594:```
プロパティを設定できません。この言語モードでは、プロパティの設定はコアの型のみでサポートされています。
