codex
1. [src/app/api/chat/route.ts](</C:/dev/akari/src/app/api/chat/route.ts:45>): duplicate sends are not idempotent. The AI SDK sends `messageId`, but the route ignores it and always inserts a fresh DB message at line 50. A retry of the same request will duplicate the user message and likely the assistant reply. Suggested fix: store the client message id or an idempotency key in `messages`, add a unique constraint on `(conversation_id, client_message_id, role)`, and upsert/skip duplicates.

2. [src/app/api/chat/route.ts](</C:/dev/akari/src/app/api/chat/route.ts:45>): the user message is persisted before provider/model resolution and before the stream succeeds. If `resolveModel`, `convertToModelMessages`, or the provider request fails, the DB keeps an orphan user message; retrying then duplicates it. Suggested fix: validate and resolve first, then persist in an idempotent transaction, or persist a `pending/failed` status and update it on stream completion.

3. [src/app/api/chat/route.ts](</C:/dev/akari/src/app/api/chat/route.ts:8>): request validation only checks `messages` is an array of `unknown`, then casts to `UIMessage[]` at line 34. Malformed `parts` can throw in `extractText`, and invalid/tool/file messages can reach `convertToModelMessages`. Suggested fix: use AI SDK v6 `safeValidateUIMessages`/`validateUIMessages` plus app limits for message count and text length before touching persistence.

4. [src/app/api/chat/route.ts](</C:/dev/akari/src/app/api/chat/route.ts:62>): provider conversion/stream setup is outside a `try/catch`, while user persistence already happened. Suggested fix: wrap conversion and `streamText` setup, return structured 4xx/5xx errors, and only commit persistence after the request is known valid.

5. [src/app/api/chat/route.ts](</C:/dev/akari/src/app/api/chat/route.ts:62>): the model context is taken from client-submitted `messages`, not the server’s stored conversation. A forged request can omit, edit, or reorder prior messages. Suggested fix: load prior messages from `listMessages(conversationId)` on the server and append only the validated new user message from the request.

6. [src/lib/db/init.ts](</C:/dev/akari/src/lib/db/init.ts:15>): `ensureDbReady` is process-local only. Two Next workers/serverless instances can both run migrations/seeding when the DB is empty, and default personas have generated ids with no uniqueness on name. Suggested fix: run migrations as a deploy/startup step, or guard lazy init with a DB/file lock and seed with stable ids plus `INSERT OR IGNORE`.

7. [src/lib/db/queries.ts](</C:/dev/akari/src/lib/db/queries.ts:91>): `appendMessage` inserts the message and updates the conversation in two separate statements. A failure between them leaves stale `updatedAt`; concurrent delete can also surface as a late FK error. Suggested fix: wrap insert + conversation update in a Drizzle transaction.

8. [src/lib/db/queries.ts](</C:/dev/akari/src/lib/db/queries.ts:87>): messages are ordered only by `createdAt`. Multiple messages can share the same millisecond, so replay order can become nondeterministic. Suggested fix: add a monotonic sequence column or order by `createdAt, id`.

9. [src/lib/db/queries.ts](</C:/dev/akari/src/lib/db/queries.ts:101>): `recentMessagesForChat` is misleading if used later: it orders ascending then limits, returning the oldest 50, not recent messages. Suggested fix: order descending, limit, then reverse in memory before sending to the model.

10. [vitest.config.ts](</C:/dev/akari/vitest.config.ts:13>): coverage explicitly excludes `src/app/**`, which excludes `/api/chat`; there are no route tests for persistence, duplicate sends, malformed bodies, provider failures, or stream finish behavior. Suggested fix: include route handlers in coverage and add unit tests that mock `streamText`, `resolveModel`, and DB queries.

11. [src/app/layout.tsx](</C:/dev/akari/src/app/layout.tsx:49>): the FOUC script is static and validates localStorage values, so the inline content is not directly user-injectable, but it requires `unsafe-inline` unless you add a CSP nonce/hash. Suggested fix: wire a nonce through the layout or use a hashed static script in CSP.

12. [src/components/theme/theme-provider.tsx](</C:/dev/akari/src/components/theme/theme-provider.tsx:31>): the provider hydrates with `theme='system'` and `resolvedTheme='light'` even when the pre-hydration script applied dark mode. The page class avoids full-page FOUC, but the toggle icon/state can flash wrong until effects run. Suggested fix: initialize client state from `localStorage`/`matchMedia` with a lazy initializer or hide the toggle until mounted.

13. [src/app/chat/[id]/chat-client.tsx](</C:/dev/akari/src/app/chat/[id]/chat-client.tsx:79>): the chat textarea has no accessible label; placeholder text is not a label. Suggested fix: add `aria-label="Message"` or a visually hidden `<label>`.

14. [src/components/chat/message-bubble.tsx](</C:/dev/akari/src/components/chat/message-bubble.tsx:28>): markdown rendering relies on `react-markdown` defaults. That is safer than `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`, but security depends on not adding `rehype-raw` later and on URL sanitization behavior. Suggested fix: explicitly set an allowlist for elements/URL protocols and add XSS regression tests for raw HTML and `javascript:` links.

15. [src/app/personas/actions.ts](</C:/dev/akari/src/app/personas/actions.ts:14>): `systemPrompt` and `model` are effectively unbounded/arbitrary server-side inputs. A direct Server Action call can store huge prompts or unsupported/expensive model ids. Suggested fix: add max lengths and validate `model` belongs to the selected provider’s catalog.

16. [src/app/chat/actions.ts](</C:/dev/akari/src/app/chat/actions.ts:28>) and [src/app/personas/actions.ts](</C:/dev/akari/src/app/personas/actions.ts:62>): destructive Server Actions have no authentication/authorization boundary. If this is deployed beyond a single-user local app, anyone who can reach the app can mutate/delete conversations and personas. Suggested fix: add auth or explicitly mark/enforce local-only deployment.

17. [src/app/chat/[id]/chat-client.tsx](</C:/dev/akari/src/app/chat/[id]/chat-client.tsx:31>): a new `DefaultChatTransport` is created on every render. If `useChat` treats transport identity as meaningful, typing can cause unnecessary churn. Suggested fix: wrap transport creation in `useMemo([conversationId])`.

18. [src/app/chat/[id]/chat-client.tsx](</C:/dev/akari/src/app/chat/[id]/chat-client.tsx:64>): every input keystroke re-renders every message and reruns markdown rendering. Suggested fix: memoize `MessageBubble` and split the composer state into a child component.

19. [src/app/chat/[id]/chat-client.tsx](</C:/dev/akari/src/app/chat/[id]/chat-client.tsx:66>): API errors are shown visually but not announced to assistive tech. Suggested fix: render errors in a `role="alert"`/`aria-live="polite"` region.

20. Production readiness gap: there are no route-level `error.tsx`/`loading.tsx` files under `src/app/chat` or `src/app/personas`, and `/api/chat` has no structured logging/observability around provider errors or failed DB writes. Suggested fix: add app error boundaries/loading states and log provider/DB failures with conversation id and message idempotency key.

I did not see direct SQL injection: DB access is through Drizzle query builders rather than string-concatenated SQL.
